{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790348155,"nonce":"f8HO+JBiSl/LnZx10mV967nX9bY=","title":"Bytecode header: the checksum skips the header, and payload_size, flags, padding and minor version are never checked","message":"The CRC32 covers only the payload, bytes 44 to the end (crates/compiler/src/bytecode.rs:678, :693). A flipped format or version byte passes, and a flipped format byte decodes the payload with the wrong codec.\n\npayload_size is written (:680) but the reader takes bytes[44..] whatever the field says (:701-709), so trailing garbage or a truncated file is only caught if the codec happens to fail. flags (:585, always 0), the three padding bytes (:766-768) and the minor version (:593-606) are never validated.\n\nThe reader should check payload_size against the file length, refuse non-zero padding and unknown flag bits, and either extend the checksum over the header (minus the checksum field) or checksum the header separately.","files":null}]}